    <p class="kicker">THE WHY</p>
    <h1 class="display">Somebody had to keep the tape.</h1>
  </header>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>I started LiquidSea because Southeast Asia's private-market deal flow was scattered across press releases, paywalled trackers and group chats — and none of them told you what a round actually <em>meant</em>. The global business press covers this region in one paragraph a quarter. The deals deserve better records than that.</p>
    <p>So every week I collect each disclosed fundraise across Singapore, Thailand, Vietnam, Indonesia, the Philippines and Malaysia, verify it against a primary source, and publish it with a short, honest note — including when I think a round is overhyped. The digest is free. The data lives openly in a public repository, machine-readable, so it outlasts any newsletter platform.</p>
    <p>The events calendar exists for the same reason: the real business of this region happens at meetups in Saigon and side events in Singapore, not on social media. If you know a deal or an event I've missed, <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">my inbox is open</a>.</p>
